DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260829T210000
UID:bd3083e938893b2c73fa494339a300bd@mobilize.us
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://mobilize-uploads-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/u
 ploads/organization/Mobilize%20Generalized%20Indivisible%20Event%20Campaig
 n%20Image%202_20231214173755488494.png
DESCRIPTION:An Ordinary Insanity\, Daniel Ellsberg's last work and the Vet
 erans For Peace Golden Rule Project - 2 short films Daniel Ellsberg's job 
 at the Defense Dept. was "the design of nuclear war plans." He thought it 
 was "the most evil planning in the history of humanity." That changed ever
 ything for him. Join us for a screening of 2 short films: _An Ordinary Ins
 anity_\, based upon interviews at the end of Ellsberg's life\, and _Golden
  Rule: The Journey for Peace_\, about the Veterans For Peace Golden Rule
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA\
 , 95472
URL:https://www.mobilize.us/indivisible/event/1009009/
X-SOURCE:Indivisible Sonoma County (Mobilize)
END:VEVENT
